# ---------------------------------------------------------------- verdicts
# Winoracle x64 output above (x86 identical). Vitreo before the fix: 468 diff
# lines x64 / x86 (2DMS SRVs over one sample E_NOTIMPL, buffer RTVs E_NOTIMPL,
# the R32 cast / mip UAV of a volume not bound, comparison border .5
# E_NOTIMPL, every alpha-AA / quadrilateral line drawn aliased, aliased lines
# on 4x covered per sample). After: 2, "vol R32_UINT cast mip0 W{1,1} mark
# mip1 z0": WARP's view is one W slice, yet its threads z=1 wrote past it
# into mip 1 ("a0010000 a0010001 ..."), which D3D leaves undefined (an
# out-of-bounds UAV write is dropped, as Vitreo does).
# ms1: a one-sample Texture2DMS reads its one sample for EVERY sample index
#   (cs[18] sample 1, cs[19] sample 3 = texel (1,1)); samplepos is (0,0) for
#   index 0 and 1; GetDimensions reports 1 sample.
# bufrt: only the window's elements change, at any texel-aligned
#   FirstElement (12 bytes for RGBA8 {3,5}, 10 for R16 {5,3}).
# cmp: the border's red is compared as a float, unclamped even for R16_UNORM
#   (border 1.5: ref .9 < 1.5 passes).
# line: alpha-AA = a 4-wide rectangle (edges through centres by the top-left
#   rule) with o0.a *= clamp(0.675 - 0.45 d); quadrilateral = a 1.4-wide
#   rectangle; both on 1x targets, through a GS, for wireframe edges; lines
#   face front; aliased and alpha-AA lines on 4x write every sample of a
#   covered pixel (the 4x grids equal the 1x ones), quadrilateral lines are
#   covered per sample.
